      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "The two star fillies hold the key. Must go with the Flight Stakes winner GLOBAL GOAL (8) who took a while to stoke up in that Group 1 last start but really knuckled down late. Perfectly placed out to this distance now and with the weight pull on the boys she can score again. PROXIMA DEA (9) looked dead and buried in the Gloaming last time out but came again in the final 100m to just arrive and keep her 100% record intact. That followed a six-week break so she can only improve. No risk she is up to this. STORMY MARCO (5) is the pick of the males after his eye-catching effort on the Gloaming, beaten just half a length after coming from next to last. Tommy Berry will ride him cold and let go topping the rise. Genuine contender. SCAROLE (3) has form around most key rivals and looks ready to tackle this longer journey. DIAMETER (1) is a half-brother to Cylinder so 2000m might be a stretch. Multiples only.",
